{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_11-29-07-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, collections\nsrc=json.load(open('map-v3.json'), object_pairs_hook=collections.OrderedDict)\nsrc['version']=3\nfor b in src['behaviors']:\n    if b['id']=='b-elect-self':\n        b['important_branches'][2]=(\\\"the self-vote is persisted for the proposed term without comparing it with the record that may already exist for that term, \\\"\n            \\\"and the transfer path keeps pre-vote from filtering this campaign, so a published term that has dropped below a recorded vote's term lets the \\\"\n            \\\"campaign propose exactly that term, overwrite the record and collect a quorum while another voter's record for it is still empty\\\")\n        b['unknowns']=[\\\"whether the dual leadership of one term can be made to persist, and whether two leaders of one term can commit conflicting entries\\\"]\nfor f in src['facts']:\n    if f['id'] in ('f-term-adopted','f-vote-record'):\n        f['unknowns']=[]\nsrc['core_overview']['rationale']=(\\\"Both core relationships and their connection are explained from actual code: formation and advancement are grounded in the vote \\\"\n    \\\"tally, the pre-vote round, commitment.match/recalculate and the startIndex own-term rule; context and authority are grounded in the term/state update, \\\"\n    \\\"leader identity update, the leader lease step-down and TimeoutNow. The connection is sourced: votes are only re-granted for the same term, older-term \\\"\n    \\\"RPCs are ignored, match indexes are only usable at or after startIndex, and a transfer requires the target to be caught up. Three mechanisms that \\\"\n    \\\"earlier versions of this map left as unknowns are now recorded where they belong: the transport heartbeat callback performs its term, state and leader \\\"\n    \\\"writes without being serialized with the main goroutine and publishes the term through a plain atomic store; a client future for VerifyLeader or a \\\"\n    \\\"batched Apply carries no shutdown escape once a completed Shutdown has left the buffered request channels unprocessed; and the candidate's self-vote is \\\"\n    \\\"written for the proposed term without comparing it with the vote record, so a published term that has dropped by one makes the next election propose a \\\"\n    \\\"term that already holds a vote and overwrite it while the transfer exemption keeps the campaign from being filtered. The third links to the first: the \\\"\n    \\\"overwritten record is the only barrier the vote path's exemption leaves, so the only questions still open on this line are whether the resulting dual \\\"\n    \\\"leadership can be made to persist and whether it can commit conflicting entries. The counter-parts that bound each mechanism are recorded beside them \\\"\n    \\\"(the fast path cannot append logs or advance the commit index; the default unbuffered applyCh always completes and the leader lease and the replication \\\"\n    \\\"path cover term discovery; the vote-granting path still refuses a second different vote in one term and a leader refuses a transfer request whose vote it \\\"\n    \\\"already recorded), so no core gap is claimed and the overview stays usable.\\\")\nopen('map-v4.json','w').write(json.dumps(src, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nprint('written')\nPY\npython3 -c \\\"\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('map-v4.json'))\nprint('version',m['version'],'behaviors',len(m['behaviors']),'facts',len(m['facts']),'surfaces',len(m['surfaces']))\nfor f in m['facts']:\n    if f['id'] in ('f-term-adopted','f-vote-record'): print(f['id'],'unknowns',f['unknowns'])\nb=[x for x in m['behaviors'] if x['id']=='b-elect-self'][0]; print('elect unknowns',b['unknowns'])\nprint('overview',m['core_overview']['status'],m['core_overview']['core_gaps'])\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
